            },
            {
                "name": "Note",
                "type": "digsim.circuit.components.Note",
                "display_name": "Note",
                "settings": {
                    "text": "Two walkie-talkies, the same Verilog module (examples/yosys_inout/walkie_talkie.v),\nshare one 4-bit bus wire. Their bus port, the diamond, is an inout port:\nit can send on the wire and listen to it.\n\n1. Start the simulation and set a message with the switches of walkie-talkie A.\n2. Hold Talk A (key 1): A sends, and both displays show the message.\n3. Hold Talk B (key 2) instead: the same wire carries B's message the other way.\n4. Hold both with different messages: a collision, the bus is undefined (X, red).\nWith nobody talking the bus is not driven (Z, blue), and the displays are blank."
                }
            }
        ]
    },
